    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0222" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg114"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson officially confirms the successes of the Government at Bage and
                    reports the continuance of the fighting at Nictheroy. He transmits the
                    information received by him that the <hi rendition="#italic">Nictheroy</hi> and
                    two other war vessels of the Government sailed from Pernambuco for the south on
                    the 20th, and says that the situation remains unchanged.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
